# 10 — Lookup table: a nonlinear relationship you draw, not derive.
# Some relationships aren't a tidy formula — they're a curve. A table maps an
# input to an output through breakpoints, interpolating between them and
# clamping at the ends. Here the drain rate rises nonlinearly with the level.
stock Water [liters] = 80

param inflow = 4
table drainCurve = (0,0) (20,1) (40,4) (60,9) (80,16)

flow draining = drainCurve(Water)

change(Water) = inflow - draining

sim dt=0.1 to=40 method=rk4
plot Water, draining
